      <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
        <tr valign="middle"> 
          <td colspan="2" height="30" background="newsheader.jpg"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4"><b><font size="5">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;MISSING: Various Mobs from Velious and Kunark...</font></b></font></td>
        </tr>
        <tr bgcolor="#330033"> 
          <td width="60%"><font size="2"><i><font face="Verdana">by <A href="javascript:createWindow('memberdetails.asp?id=1','profile','scrollbars,width=550,height=500')"><font color=yellow>Falqour Thornwalker</font></a></font></i></font></td>
          <td width="40%"> 
            <div align="right"><font size="2"><b>Posted: 4/7/2002 3:03:34 AM</b></font></div>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td colspan="2">
<font face="Verdana" size="2"><B>The Spirits of Fire lay waste to multiple villains in a night of bloodshed - and they got pictures…                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   </B></font><P>
<font face="Verdana" size="2"><p align="center"><font face="Verdana">To commemorate our guild's recent Grand Reformation, the newly reformed Spirits of Fire journeyed forth to fulfill our holy mandate - keel stuff. Below is a photo documentary detailing our steps through the fun time we had tonight. Enjoy!</font></p><p align="center"><font face="Verdana" size="5">Journey to Velketor's Labyrinth</font></p><p align="center"><font face="Verdana" size="2">Why? Well, to kill the Sorcerer, of course.</font></p><p align="center">&nbsp;</p><p align="center"><font face="Verdana"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/april6th1.jpg" width="400" height="300"><br><i><font size="5">The Art of Zen Pulling</font></i><br><b><font size="2">The monks prepare for the solo pull</font></b><br><font size="2">(Left: Matthi, purdy human / Right: Sssilence, smelly leezard)</font></font></p><hr><p align="center"> <font face="Verdana"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/april6th2.jpg" width="400" height="300"><br><i><font size="5">&quot;We've Got Incoming!&quot;</font></i> <br><b><font size="2">In response to their master's slaying, Velketor's minions descend upon the camp, and are easily dispatched<br></font></b></font></p><hr><p align="center"><font face="Verdana"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/april6th3.jpg" width="500" height="375"><br><i><font size="5">SoF the Sorcerer</font></i><br><b><font size="2">The Spirits of Fire hold a small gathering in the former throne room of the Master of the Labyrinth</font></b></font></p><hr><p align="center"><font face="Verdana"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/april6th4.jpg" width="400" height="300"><br><i><font size="5">Battleplans</font></i><br><font size="2"><b>The night is young, and our agenda needs filling</b><br>(Middle Foreground: Belin)</font></font></p><hr><p align="center"><font face="Verdana"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/april6th5.jpg" width="300" height="225"><br><i><font size="5">Tracking the Enemy</font></i><br><font size="2"><b>Our druids inform us that Lord Dolijonijiarnimorinar is up.. We'll have to change that</b><br>(Center: Kharpern)</font></font></p><hr><p align="center"><font face="Verdana"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/april6th6.jpg" width="500" height="375"><br><i><font size="5">Lord Doljonijiarnimorinar is Down</font></i><br><font size="2"><b>One less semi-uber mob to terrorize the poor Lower Dogs campers</b><br>(Right, kneeling over Doljo's corpse: Moonwolf.. odd, usually it's the other way around...)</font></font></p><hr><p align="center"><font face="Verdana"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/april6th7.jpg" width="400" height="300"><br><i><font size="5">The Night is Still Young</font></i><br><font size="2"><b>As the guild contemplates it's next move, our resident Skyfire camper, Herrick, makes an interesting discovery...</b></font></font></p><hr><p align="center"><font face="Verdana"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/april6th8.jpg" width="400" height="300"><br><i><font size="5">Talendor is Up</font></i><br><font size="2"><b>The Guild races to Skyfire to assist Herrick - he still has a headache from having Tale fall on him</b><br>(Far left: Mckenna)</font></font></p><hr><p align="center"><font face="Verdana"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/april6th9.jpg" width="500" height="356"><br><i><font size="5">Talendor Fights Bravely</font></i><br><b><font size="2">But, in the end, he didn't win. Moonie looted the corpse so fast, I couldn't get any shots of his big bloated corpse. Ah well, next time...</font></b></font></p><hr><p align="center"><font face="Verdana"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/april6th10.jpg" width="400" height="300"><br><i><font size="5">Conversations with Charisa</font></i><br><font size="2"><b>Meanwhile, back on Velious, Quixie holds a meeting with Scout Charisa, and the guild responds to aid her in her quest</b><br>(Left: Scout Charisa - helpful NPC / Right: Quxeos - she likes cookies)</font><br></font></p><hr><p align="center"><font face="Verdana"> </font></p><p align="center"><font face="Verdana"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/april6th11.jpg" width="500" height="375"><br><i><font size="5">FEE FI FO PHOOEY</font></i><br><font size="2"><b>The Kromzek Captain gets his butt handed to him by SoF</b><br>(Left Foreground: Meridaen - guest star tanker / Right Foreground: A_Kromzek_Captain)</font></font></p><hr><p align="center"><font face="Verdana"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/april6th12.jpg" width="350" height="358"><br><i><font size="5">The Gods are Amused</font></i><br><font size="2"><b>Lulabye, the Princess of Zeb, stops by to watch and chat</b><br>(Center: Lulabye (GM)- not currently a gnome, or teapot - heckuva dresser, though.)</font></font></p><hr><p align="center"><font face="Verdana"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/april6th13.jpg" width="300" height="376"><br><font size="5">A Reward Fit for a Queen</font><br><font size="2"><b>Quixie, looking sharp as ever</b><br>(Center: Quxeos - not currently eating a cake)</font></font></p><hr><p align="center"><font face="Verdana" size="3" color="#FFFF00">All in all, it was a fine night. Grats to everyone who got lootz!</font></p>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              </font>
</td>
